Here's a thought for a feature. I haven't read all the 3.1 ideas that have
been floating around, but I have seen references to a 'Mall level' that got
praised/trashed. This is a twist on the mall idea.

Since many of the elements of Nethack are based on references to popular
fantasy and sci-fi works, how about paying homage to the 'Myth' books by
Robert Aspirin and create a tool called a '4D hopper' that can take you
to the bazaar at Deva. The act of transporting would probably be a serious
hit to your power so you couldn't do it often. Or, perhaps a wand with 0 or
1 charges in it (get stranded at the bazaar at deva and have to work your
way out).

The bazaar is a place to buy anything your heart desires. I couldn't imagine
you being able to steal anything, because Deveels are notoriously suspicious.
Everything would come at a premium (food rations = 300 g.p's, etc), but 
everything would be for sale. You could even buy a tame baby dragon named
Gleep.

Would this make the game too easy? Maybe/probably. But it is a fun thought.

